# Financial Year Business Rules

- Only one ACTIVE Financial Year
- Name must be unique
- Start Date must be before End Date
- Closed Financial Years are read-only
- no overlay with existing end and start date while creating a new financial year
- Closing requires reconciliation
- Active Financial Years must not overlap according to business rules

# Financial Year phases
1. Create a meeting with date, place, agenda and remarks
2. Record payment transactions of each members - Contribution payment, loan repayment, Fine payment, special loan payment
3. 200 will be collected as contribution each week, if some member has due, notify it
4. Bank transactions tab- the bank investment and bank withdrawel will be recorded in meeting with transaction date
5. Income / expense will be recordered in this tab
6. SUmmary will display the bank balance, cash balance, meeting transaction summary 
7. Close meeting, and current time will be saved as close time
8. States - Draft, in progress, approved, closed


# Feature Development Order
1. Meetings
2. Attendance
3. Bank transactions
4. Contributions payment
5. Loans repayment
6. Loan disbursal

